NetHack, with its tty interface, requires only the C library and
termcap library, and not any Carbon or Qt. However, NetHack also needs
to use system calls to communicate with the operating system kernel.

For example, a PPC 32 port for OpenBSD would make system calls to the
OpenBSD kernel. NetHack needs system calls to access files and
devices. This port would not work with Linux, because the Linux kernel
does not understand the OpenBSD system calls. Therefore, any PPC port
will require a specific operating system.

Many PPC operating systems provide NetHack in their repositories. To
obtain NetHack, you would look at the repositories, not at www.nethack.org

For example, to install NetHack for OpenBSD/powerpc, I would start at
http://www.openbsd.org/4.1_packages/ and choose powerpc, then look for
nethack in the list. To install NetHack for NetBSD/powerpc or Linux/
powerpc, I would have to look elsewhere.

